{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 81,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sing aloud unto God our strength:\nMake a joyful noise unto the God of Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Raise a song, and bring hither the timbrel,\nThe pleasant harp with the psaltery.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blow the trumpet at the new moon,\nAt the full moon, on our feast-day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it is a statute for Israel,\nAn ordinance of the God of Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He appointed it in Joseph for a testimony,\nWhen he went out over the land of Egypt,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Where",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I heard a language that I knew not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I removed his shoulder from the burden:\nHis hands were freed from the basket.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou calledst in trouble, and I delivered thee;\nI answered thee in the secret place of thunder;\nI proved thee at the waters of Meribah. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear, O my people, and I will testify unto thee:\nO Israel, if thou wouldest hearken unto me!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There shall no strange god be in thee;\nNeither shalt thou worship any foreign god.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am Jehovah thy God,\nWho brought thee up out of the land of Egypt:\nOpen thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But my people hearkened not to my voice;\nAnd Israel would none of me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So I let them go after the stubbornness of their heart,\nThat they might walk in their own counsels.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that my people would hearken unto me,\nThat Israel would walk in my ways!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would soon subdue their enemies,\nAnd turn my hand against their adversaries.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The haters of Jehovah should submit themselves unto him:\nBut their time should endure for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.81.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He would feed them also with the finest of the wheat;\nAnd with honey out of the rock would I satisfy thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "God’s goodness and Israel’s waywardness.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "For the Chief Musician; set to the Gittith. A Psalm of Asaph.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
